'''Esport Academy Copenhagen''' (fomerly known as '''Preasy Esport''' and '''Ambush By Preasy DK''') is a [[:Category:Denmark|Danish]] professional esports organization. 

Preasy, a subsidiary of electricity company Energive, entered professional ''Counter-Strike'' in a merger with esports organization [[Ambush]], which they revived through their sponsorship, on 23 April 2023. <ref name="Preasy">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Ambush_gg/status/1650077111472775168|date=2023-04-23|title=PRESS RELEASE|author=[[Ambush]]}}</ref> The two organizations split ways just a month later on 7 June 2023. <ref name="Preasy2">{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/Ambush_gg/status/1666398398516281345|date=2023-06-07|title=Ambush By Preasy Closes, Ambush Resurrects And "By Preasy" Becomes Preasy Esport|author='''Ambush'''}}</ref> [[Ambush]] retained the international roster, while Preasy kept the Danish lineup and renamed the organization to '''Preasy Esport'''.

The organization was revived under the name "Esport Academy Copenhagen" following [[AaB esport]]'s departure from professional ''Counter-Strike 2'' on May 14th, 2026.

